  "grammar": {
    "explain": [
      "This is the lesson that makes Georgian sound Georgian. Five sounds come in pairs: one with a puff of air, as in English, and one *tight*, with no air at all. In Latin letters the tight one gets an apostrophe: *k'*, *t'*, *p'*, *ch'*, *ts'*.",
      "How to make a tight sound: close your throat as if you were holding your breath, say the consonant, and let it go with a small pop. Put your hand in front of your mouth: with ქ you feel air, with კ you don't.",
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "with air",
            "tight, no air",
            "example"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "ქ *k*",
              "კ *k'*",
              "ქალაქი *kalaki* (city) · კატა *k'at'a* (cat)"
            ],
            [
              "თ *t*",
              "ტ *t'*",
              "თბილისი *tbilisi* · ტბა *t'ba* (lake)"
            ],
            [
              "ფ *p*",
              "პ *p'*",
              "ფული *puli* (money) · პური *p'uri* (bread)"
            ],
            [
              "ჩ *ch*",
              "ჭ *ch'*",
              "ჩაი *chai* (tea) · ჭიქა *ch'ika* (glass)"
            ],
            [
              "ც *ts*",
              "წ *ts'*",
              "ცა *tsa* (sky) · წიგნი *ts'igni* (book)"
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      "The difference changes the meaning, so it's worth practising: but don't worry if it takes time. Georgians will understand you anyway.",
      {
        "h": "With air"
      },
      {
        "letters": [
          {
            "letter": "ქ",
            "latin": "k",
            "say": "like the k in kit, with a puff of air",
            "word": "ქალაქი",
            "word_latin": "kalaki",
            "meaning": "city"
          },
          {
            "letter": "ფ",
            "latin": "p",
            "say": "like the p in pen, with a puff of air",
            "word": "ფული",
            "word_latin": "puli",
            "meaning": "money"
          },
          {
            "letter": "ჩ",
            "latin": "ch",
            "say": "like the ch in church, with a puff of air",
            "word": "ჩაი",
            "word_latin": "chai",
            "meaning": "tea"
          },
          {
            "letter": "ც",
            "latin": "ts",
            "say": "like the ts in cats, with a puff of air",
            "word": "ცა",
            "word_latin": "tsa",
            "meaning": "sky"
          }
        ],
        "lang": "ka"
      },
      {
        "h": "Tight, with no air"
      },
      {
        "letters": [
          {
            "letter": "კ",
            "latin": "k'",
            "say": "a tight k, with no air: hold your breath and let it pop",
            "word": "კატა",
            "word_latin": "k'at'a",
            "meaning": "cat"
          },
          {
            "letter": "ტ",
            "latin": "t'",
            "say": "a tight t, with no air",
            "word": "ტბა",
            "word_latin": "t'ba",
            "meaning": "lake"
          },
          {
            "letter": "პ",
            "latin": "p'",
            "say": "a tight p, with no air",
            "word": "პური",
            "word_latin": "p'uri",
            "meaning": "bread"
          },
          {
            "letter": "ჭ",
            "latin": "ch'",
            "say": "a tight ch, with no air",
            "word": "ჭიქა",
            "word_latin": "ch'ika",
            "meaning": "glass (for drinking)"
          },
          {
            "letter": "წ",
            "latin": "ts'",
            "say": "a tight ts, with no air",
            "word": "წიგნი",
            "word_latin": "ts'igni",
            "meaning": "book"
          }
        ],
        "lang": "ka"
      },
      {
